# mm.display

A portable display lifecycle and packed-region interface. Graphics policy,
fonts, image decoding, and controller commands live above or below this module,
not inside it.

One-bit pixels are row-major and byte-aligned per row: the most significant bit
is leftmost, one is white, zero is black, and padding at the visible right edge
has no portable meaning. write changes controller memory; refresh changes the
visible panel.

The platform-interface marker makes a selected board display provider part of
an executable only when its ordinary closure reaches mm.display. Host tests may
replace the linkable Unsupported fallback directly.
